   $q$Which is the vertex form of $y = -2x^2 - 8x + 3$?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$y = -2(x + 2)^2 + 7$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"compensated-without-multiplying-by-a"},{"text":"$y = -2(x - 2)^2 + 11$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"flipped-sign-of-h"},{"text":"$y = -2(x + 2)^2 + 3$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"forgot-to-compensate"},{"text":"$y = -2(x + 2)^2 + 11$","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$y = -2(x + 2)^2 + 11$$q$, $q$Factor $-2$ from the $x$ terms: $y = -2(x^2 + 4x) + 3$. Add $4$ inside the parentheses and compensate outside:$y = -2(x^2 + 4x + 4) + 8 + 3$, because the added $4$ is really $-2 \cdot 4 = -8$, which must be undone with $+8$. So $y = -2(x + 2)^2 + 11$. Check: at $x = -2$, $-2(4) + 16 + 3 = 11$. The choice ending in $+ 7$ undoes only $4$ instead of $8$.$q$, 'draft', null)
